  "That file is not a backup.": "",
  "The access key has changed.": "",
  "The ADI-2 answers again": "",
  "The ADI-2 counts as off when its USB connection disappears or it stops answering – standby, power off, USB cable unplugged, MIDI Control switched off. No wiring needed. Switching the ADI-2 on does not start the Pi again; for that use the 12 V trigger (Pi 4/3).": "",
  "The ADI-2 has answered without a break since ADI-2-Pi started.": "",
  "The ADI-2 is not answering – a snapshot would only repeat old values.": "",
  "The ADI-2 is not answering.": "",
  "The ADI-2 is on (USB), but GPIO{0} gets no trigger signal – check the wiring": "",
  "the ADI-2 is switched on or reconnects": "",
  "The ADI-2 runs at": "",
  "The ADI-2 stopped answering": "",
  "The ADI-2 switches to the rate of what plays – 44.1 kHz for AirPlay and Bluetooth, up to 192 kHz from UPnP, Squeezelite or Roon. It mutes briefly when it switches.": "",
  "the ADI-2’s Trigger Out is wired to GPIO3": "",
  "the ADI-2’s Trigger Out is wired to GPIO3 – with it, switching the ADI-2 on also starts the Pi": "",
  "The ADI-2's USB audio device was not found on the Pi.": "",
  "the analog input": "",
  "The audio service (adi2-pi-audio) is not running, so the receivers wait for it.": "",
  "the audio service is not running": "",
  "The audio service is not running.": "",
  "the battery supplies the Pi": "",
  "The best codec both sides support is used: LDAC, aptX HD, aptX, SBC-XQ or SBC to headphones; aptX HD, aptX, SBC-XQ or SBC from phones (iPhones use SBC – AAC isn't available on Raspberry Pi OS).": "",
  "The editor is a scratch pad: nothing reaches the unit until you apply or store it.": "",
  "The name must not be empty (letters, digits and simple punctuation).": "",
  "The newest is heard": "",
  "The others are muted until it stops; then the one before is heard again.": "",
  "The outputs play the first input in the list that has a signal: when it loses its signal they switch to the next one, and back when it returns. AES and SPDIF are detected; Analog and USB can’t be, so the list ends with them. A source picked by hand stays until a signal comes or goes. While the Pi plays on USB, the output comes back to the input chosen here.": "",
  "the Pi has played nothing for {0} min": "",
  "the Pi shuts down after {0} unless the ADI-2 is switched on. Restarting ADI-2-Pi later doesn’t count as a start.": "",
  "the Pi starts playing": "",
  "the Pi stays on. It only shuts down after it has seen the ADI-2 on and then off.": "",
  "the Pi stops playing": "",
  "The Pi's Bluetooth shares its antenna with Wi-Fi on 2.4 GHz. For dropout-free LDAC, connect the Pi by Ethernet or use 5 GHz Wi-Fi.": "",
  "The preamp becomes the channel gain.": "",
  "the release archive and its signature, without the Pi going online": "",
  "the same version as installed": "",
  "The signature file (.tar.gz.sig) is missing – choose both files at once.": "",
  "the unit loads its stored copy": "",
  "The unit reports nothing beyond RME’s table.": "",
  "The unit sends all its settings; these aren’t in RME’s MIDI table (v0.2). To find out what one is, change a setting on the unit that ADI-2-Pi doesn’t show – the line that belongs to it lights up here. Copy report puts the list in a text, e.g. for an issue report.": "",
  "The volume limits above still apply. Mute on the sender mutes the outputs. Changing the volume on the ADI-2 doesn’t move the sender’s slider. Switching this on or off restarts AirPlay and Spotify Connect. UPnP, Squeezelite, Snapcast and Bluetooth keep their own volume.": "",
